    {
      "run": 3,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "As I look back on my journey, I can barely believe the small, cramped spaces I've navigated. I started in a galley, a narrow kitchen area filled with the pungent scent of salt and the faint hum of stale air. It was there that I first noticed a kettle, its tin body dented from years of use. I've since picked up that kettle, as well as a coil of rope that was stiff with salt, and a brass key that I found on a landing with a peculiar window.\n\nMy travels have taken me through a store, a workshop, and now, it seems, up to a stairway. The rope and key are now in my possession, and I wonder what doors they might unlock, or what uses they might serve in the days to come. For now, I stand at the foot of the stair, the cool air of the landing a welcome respite from the cramped, dimly lit spaces that came before.",
